the PC gaming ecosystem is easily the  largest in the industry with tens of  thousands of games available to play Not  only that unlike switch or Playstation  there isn't exactly a first party  publisher on PC which means there are a  few true Marquee exclusive games on the  platform but in cases where  multi-platform games do appear we  believe that they're best played on PC  and deserve a spot on this list  at first glance neon white can be hard  to comprehend I mean I have no idea  what's going on here with its first  person gameplay that mixes speed running  in a castle-like heaven World along with  a card based mechanic the game may not  seem initially intuitive like who knows  what to do with cards I certainly don't  yet once you dive into the world of the  game it quickly becomes one of the most  fluid experiences out there the beauty  of neon white is in its details as it's  quickly obvious how subtly wonderful its  design is at full speed leaping sliding  and air dashing all to shave off  milliseconds provides an arcade-like  experience and thrill on its own and the  added wrinkle of Gunplay allows for  plenty of right answers to be discovered  on the way to neon white leaderboards  immortality despite each level only  lasting a few minutes at most sometimes  even a few seconds you'll lose hours to  it as you keep trying to one-up your  previous best time I literally lost an  entire night just trying to get one more  second shaved off of my time and earned  that platinum trophy there's nothing  else quite like it and you'll be doing  yourself a massive disservice if you  don't at least give it a try  if you've ever appreciated the before  and after visual differences of mowing a  lawn mopping a floor or of course power  washing a shed then power wash simulator  is the game for you my friend in power  wash simulator you're kick-starting your  business as a power washer for hire  taking your incredibly powerful hoses to  any backyard or garage that's paying  there's something so simple yet  gratifying in watching the grime  Disappear by your hands and the game  cleverly offers a depth that takes it to  the next level but as lighthearted as it  feels its simulation gameplay is quite  detailed and when played in Co-op  especially you'll likely find an  appreciation for its strangely soothing  gameplay loop at its best power wash  simulator is a quiet relaxing experience  that's best enjoyed in small doses it's  time consuming yes but once in a while  we all need something to consume our  time  in the case of the golden idol many  players have found The Heir Apparent to  return of the Opera Dean it's a game  that devilishly obscures the truth from  you at every turn which makes uncovering  its many Secrets all the more satisfying  with a unique and even bizarre art style  the mystery game is as visually striking  as it is confounding if played with all  the answers you could see the whole game  in under two hours but to do it that way  would rob you of what makes golden idol  so memorable golden idol is a game that  quickly teaches you to think for  yourself you'll explore the  point-and-click world through several  differently styled puzzles including  interviewing Witnesses and judging their  claims piecing together notes that are  missing key information and simply  reading items like notes and newspapers  that can peel out context until  eventually you have your aha moment the  entire game feels like one big notebook  of Clues allowing you to comb through  each one on hand until the mystery is  unraveled  with the studios returning Wallace and  grommet-esque art style a sense of humor  and lightheartedness seen in every  corner of the game and a deep Suite of  features and mechanic two-point campus  takes the Sim genre to The Fairly novel  territory of a school campus and makes  it compelling for old and new players  alike building and organizing a  successful college campus could have  been the entire game but two point  Studios adds a clever depth to the  experience like managing the school's  party aspect as much as you do in your  academic intentions happy students means  tuition payments are flowing in so  creating the classroom and dorm rooms  they expect to find are Paramount and  you can create the college experience  that your college payments didn't pay  for but every college kid wants to let  loose once in a while at least and  striking that balance between  prestigious University and wild party  school makes two-point campus a funny  and sometimes unpredictable entry into  the Sim genre  two years after Call of Duty Warzone  heralded the dominating franchise's step  into the Battle Royale genre its sequel  is here to give us new modes and a new  map where the original war zone felt  like a greatest hits compilation of past  Call of Duty games war zone 2 takes  those ideas and refines them as well as  giving you a new DMZ mode a loot and  extract sandbox mode having you fight  hordes of NPCs and attempting to  infiltrate strongholds with teammates  however since Warzone 2 is new there's  still some refining to be done with  connection issues still being a problem  for some however if you're willing to  overlook the rough edges war zone 2  promises to be fun in many ways  OverWatch 2 is an extension of the  original game but that's no bad thing  OverWatch 2 did make the controversial  decision to take the series free to play  which has certainly come with its  caveats including monetization and grind  yet this also comes with increased  availability to those who can't pay up  front or at all and if you can Overlook  or ignore are those elements the base of  what makes OverWatch as a franchise  great is still here all of your favorite  heroes are in the game and this  team-based shooter still feels slick and  refined to play every character feels  unique in how to play them and they also  still have an amazing personality behind  each and every one more importantly the  new additions help push OverWatch  forward as a series the new 5v5 combat  mode shrinks each team by one and Alters  the Dynamics of the fight encouraging a  much more linked team Dynamic further  the four new heroes are all excellently  designed while certainly OverWatch 2  didn't reinvent the wheel it didn't need  to to continue the series excellent  experience  Warhammer 40K dark tide is an excellent  addition to the horde-like co-op shooter  genre first and foremost the game  excellently mixes both ranged and Close  Quarters combat enemies feel weighty and  while you can try to take them out with  the game's array of ranged weapons  including electricity influenced  projectiles and assault rifles it's when  they get in close and force you to rely  on hacking and sword fighting that the  game truly feels alive the game also has  a great balance between classes forcing  you to be aware of the positives and  negatives of your choices for Warhammer  40K fans you'll definitely get a full  experience from dark tide  return to Monkey Island  the classic Point Adventure series  Monkey Island has garnered a  well-deserved place in the annals of  video game history yet it seemed like it  might remain locked in the past for the  rest of time this is why these series  return after over two decades was a true  moment for celebration and this  unexpected sequel certainly delivered  return to Monkey Island is tinged with  Nostalgia building upon the traditional  2D point-and-click Adventure style of  gameplay from Miley obtuse puzzle  solving to quirky storytelling the story  is heartwarming and tugs at the  heartstrings and it will make series  fans feel satisfied a tall feat for a  game this long in the making even  further the game is welcome to newcomers  who might find it difficult to step into  the series adding in an optional hint  system that slightly nudges you in the  right direction overall return to Monkey  Island is a welcome return to an iconic  Video Game World  the best way to describe little to the  left is cozy the game is a delightful  puzzle game centered around a  mischievous little Scamp cat who likes  to mess up your orderly world of  household items much like real cats do  each puzzle has you trying to organize  and sort your home as you try to avoid  your feline friend leading to some fun  moments as you discover the best way to  sort poke or Pride your way to the  solution it's a Charming game that will  leave you feeling satisfied at the end  of every play session  and that's our list of the best games on  PC in 2022 yet if you want to check out  what's happening on the console side  don't forget to subscribe to Gamespot so  you can check out our list of the best  PlayStation switch and Xbox games as  well as our game of the year  foreign
 

